WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:06.525
"Uh-oh," Ally thought, watching Dawn's angry face.

2
00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:09.169
"I'd better do something to restore the peace!"

3
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:15.740
She jumped up and cleared away some dishes. Then she pulled out Alpha.

4
00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:19.324
"Play a love song for Ray and Dawn, Alpha! Fast!"

5
00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:23.860
Instead, Alpha started blaring Ally's morning wake-up music.

6
00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:29.944
"Not this!" Ally whispered. "A love song—one that's good for slow dancing!"

7
00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:35.936
"Affirmative," Alpha said. But then she started playing a news station.

8
00:00:35.937 --> 00:00:39.607
"Ugh!" Ally fumbled to switch off Alpha.

9
00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:43.693
Dawn uncrossed her arms and glared at Ray.

10
00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:46.522
"You said you were considering moving to the city.

11
00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:49.347
So why did you go and buy a food truck?"

12
00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:53.602
Ray ran his fingers through his hair. "I did consider the move, Dawn.

13
00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:59.661
Long and hard. But the diner is doing great, and this is where my life is.

14
00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:03.955
I'm sorry. I don't want to move to the city."

15
00:01:03.956 --> 00:01:10.376
Dawn looked upset. But finally she let out a deep sigh.

16
00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:13.794
"I understand, even though it does make me sad.

17
00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:17.020
Mateo and I will miss you very much."

18
00:01:17.021 --> 00:01:24.475
Mateo's eyes went wide. "Um . . ." He nervously cleared his throat.

19
00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:29.014
"Sorry, Mom, but I don't want to move either. All

20
00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:34.342
my friends are here, my school, my soccer camp . . ." Dawn

21
00:01:34.343 --> 00:01:42.523
bit her lip. "Well, my fashion design business is in the city. I can't give it up now." Ally

22
00:01:42.524 --> 00:01:46.213
looked from Dawn to Ray to Mateo. The

23
00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:48.992
family was at an impasse. Ally

24
00:01:48.993 --> 00:01:55.362
had to do something to bring them together—and quickly. She

25
00:01:55.363 --> 00:02:01.178
sat down again. "Dawn, what if your new career could be here?" Dawn

26
00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:05.431
shook her head. "Sandville is a small town. The

27
00:02:05.432 --> 00:02:09.161
city is the best place for a fashion designer." "You

28
00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:12.541
could open a clothing store here," Ally said. "Kate

29
00:02:12.542 --> 00:02:17.436
is always saying this town needs a fashion upgrade." "That's

30
00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:23.283
a great idea," Ray said. "It's

31
00:02:23.284 --> 00:02:32.783
not bad," Dawn said slowly. "I'll think about it." ***

32
00:02:32.784 --> 00:02:39.275
The next morning Ally and Mateo went outside to wait for Lainie Polk's car to take them to the P.O.D.

33
00:02:39.276 --> 00:02:42.582
"Thanks for coming with me, Mateo," Ally said.

34
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:47.871
"I'm sure Lainie is nice, but I feel better knowing you'll be with me today."

35
00:02:47.872 --> 00:02:50.619
"This way I'll get to see the P.O.D. too.

36
00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:58.685
That's almost as good as traveling on it," Mateo said as a dark car pulled up.

37
00:02:58.686 --> 00:03:01.599
Ally climbed into the car first.

38
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:10.488
She looked over at the other backseat passenger, eager to finally meet the mysterious billionaire.

39
00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:15.182
"You?" Ally burst out. "You're Lainie Polk?"

40
00:03:15.183 --> 00:03:20.055
It was the customer from the diner, the woman who might be a Carparian!

41
00:03:20.056 --> 00:03:23.999
"Yep!" Lainie laughed.

42
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:31.116
Ally swallowed hard. If Lainie was a Carparian, she probably knew Ally was an Astralian.

43
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:36.033
That meant she could have told Dr. Lloyd where to find Ally!

44
00:03:36.034 --> 00:03:39.198
"I, uh, think I left something in the house."

45
00:03:39.199 --> 00:03:44.874
Ally started to climb out of the car, but the driver had come around to shut the door.

46
00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:51.694
"Sorry, we don't have all day," Lainie said. "We have a P.O.D. to launch in two days!"

47
00:03:51.695 --> 00:03:55.842
"Wait!" Ally said. "My friend Mateo is coming too."

48
00:03:55.843 --> 00:03:59.512
"Nope, this is top secret," Lainie said firmly.

49
00:03:59.513 --> 00:04:04.032
"Nobody else can know where the launch site is."

50
00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:12.619
*** As the car zoomed toward the desert, Ally tried to read Lainie's mind, but she couldn't get

51
00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:19.025
anything. Lainie smiled mischievously at her. "We're going to have quite an adventure in

52
00:04:19.026 --> 00:04:24.070
space. What did you say the other day? You can't wait to get back there?"

53
00:04:24.071 --> 00:04:31.856
"Yeah, silly me! Always joking around!" Ally faked a smile.

54
00:04:31.857 --> 00:04:34.813
"I have to find a way to escape!" she thought.

55
00:04:34.814 --> 00:04:38.707
"I could be in real danger!"

56
00:04:38.708 --> 00:04:42.525
As the car approached the desert, it slowed down.

57
00:04:42.526 --> 00:04:47.525
Ally looked out the window and saw people blocking the road.

58
00:04:47.526 --> 00:04:52.097
"What are all these people doing here?" Lainie murmured.

59
00:04:52.098 --> 00:04:56.617
"Someone probably leaked the location of my P.O.D."

60
00:04:56.618 --> 00:05:03.270
As the car crawled along, people started shouting, "Watch out for the whoopers!"

61
00:05:03.271 --> 00:05:07.519
"Oh!" Lainie laughed in relief.

62
00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.145
"They haven't found my launch site!

63
00:05:10.146 --> 00:05:14.170
They're just looking for birds." She shook her head.

64
00:05:14.171 --> 00:05:16.622
"I'll make a big donation to them.

65
00:05:16.623 --> 00:05:23.200
They can build some birdhouses or something, but they should know by now that the future is in space."

66
00:05:23.201 --> 00:05:29.226
"How can you say that?" Ally cried, suddenly forgetting to be scared of Lainie.

67
00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:32.826
"All life, everywhere, is important!"

68
00:05:32.827 --> 00:05:39.195
Lainie laughed loudly and shook her head.

69
00:05:39.196 --> 00:05:45.053
"The next thing you're going to tell me is that all people should learn to get along, right?"

70
00:05:45.054 --> 00:05:53.946
Ally gasped. "That's exactly what a Carparian would say!" she thought.

